import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy | This Week In Newsletters" description="How This Week In Newsletters uses optional analytics and how to change your cookie choice.">
  <main id="main" class="privacy-page">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>This notice covers thisweeknewsletter.com, a newsletter discovery directory by z08 Studio. Publications and the Google suggestion form have their own privacy notices.</p>
    <h2>Optional analytics</h2>
    <p>If you allow analytics, we use Google Analytics to understand visits, traffic sources, approximate location, device and browser information, scrolling, weekday and newsletter selections, and clicks on publication, issue, archive, and suggestion links. We do not send form responses, contact details, or the text you enter on other websites to Analytics. Google signals and advertising personalisation are disabled.</p>
    <p>Google Analytics loads only after you allow it. You can decline and still use the entire directory. Your cookie choice and analytics cookies last up to six months in this browser.</p>
    <h2>Your choice</h2>
    <p>Use <strong>Cookie settings</strong> in the footer to change your choice. Withdrawing consent stops further analytics collection in this browser and removes this site's Google Analytics cookies. It does not erase data already collected.</p>
    <p>Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p>
    <h2>Hosting and suggestions</h2>
    <p>The hosting and DNS providers process network information to deliver and protect the site, separately from optional analytics. Suggestions are reviewed manually; submitting a form does not automatically add a newsletter to the directory.</p>
    <p>For questions, contact <a href="https://z08studio.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">z08 Studio</a>.</p>
    <a class="archive-link" href="/">Back to the calendar</a>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
